{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:38421476 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:38421476 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":2,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"38421476","source":"MED","pmid":"38421476","pmcid":"PMC10904443","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC10904443"]},"doi":"10.1007/s00508-024-02325-5","title":"[Consensus recommendations on the diagnosis and treatment of hyponatremia from the Austrian Society for Nephrology 2024].","authorString":"Schwarz C, Lindner G, Windpessl M, Knechtelsdorfer M, Saemann MD.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Schwarz C","firstName":"Christoph","lastName":"Schwarz","initials":"C","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Innere Medizin 1, Pyhrn-Eisenwurzenklinikum, Sierningerstr. 170, 4400, Steyr, Österreich. christoph.schwarz@ooeg.at."}]}},{"fullName":"Lindner G","firstName":"Gregor","lastName":"Lindner","initials":"G","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Zentrale Notaufnahme, Kepler Universitätsklinikum GmbH, Johannes-Kepler-Universität, Linz, Österreich."}]}},{"fullName":"Windpessl M","firstName":"Martin","lastName":"Windpessl","initials":"M","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Innere Medizin IV, Klinikum Wels-Grieskirchen, Wels, Österreich."}]}},{"fullName":"Knechtelsdorfer M","firstName":"Maarten","lastName":"Knechtelsdorfer","initials":"M","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"6.Medizinische Abteilung mit Nephrologie und Dialyse, Klinik Ottakring, Wien, Österreich."}]}},{"fullName":"Saemann MD","firstName":"Marcus D","lastName":"Saemann","initials":"MD","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"6.Medizinische Abteilung mit Nephrologie und Dialyse, Klinik Ottakring, Wien, Österreich."},{"affiliation":"Medizinische Fakultät, Sigmund-Freud Universität, Wien, Österreich."}]}}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"Suppl 1","volume":"136","journalIssueId":3730972,"dateOfPublication":"2024 Feb","monthOfPublication":2,"yearOfPublication":2024,"printPublicationDate":"2024-02-01","journal":{"title":"Wiener klinische Wochenschrift","medlineAbbreviation":"Wien Klin Wochenschr","isoabbreviation":"Wien Klin Wochenschr","essn":"1613-7671","issn":"0043-5325","nlmid":"21620870R"}},"pubYear":"2024","pageInfo":"1-33","abstractText":"Hyponatremia is a disorder of water homeostasis. Water balance is maintained by the collaboration of renal function and cerebral structures, which regulate thirst mechanisms and secretion of the antidiuretic hormone. Measurement of serum-osmolality, urine osmolality and urine-sodium concentration help to diagnose the different reasons for hyponatremia. Hyponatremia induces cerebral edema and might lead to severe neurological symptoms, which need acute therapy. Also, mild forms of hyponatremia should be treated causally, or at least symptomatically. An inadequate fast increase of the serum sodium level should be avoided, because it raises the risk of cerebral osmotic demyelination. Basic pathophysiological knowledge is necessary to identify the different reasons for hyponatremia which need different therapeutic procedures.","affiliation":"Innere Medizin 1, Pyhrn-Eisenwurzenklinikum, Sierningerstr. 170, 4400, Steyr, Österreich. christoph.schwarz@ooeg.at.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"ger","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Consensus Statement","Journal Article","English Abstract"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Hyponatremia","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"DI","qualifierName":"diagnosis","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"ET","qualifierName":"etiology","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"TH","qualifierName":"therapy","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Sodium"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Water"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Nephrology"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Austria"}]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["Vasopressin","Cerebral edema","osmolality","Osmotic Demyelination Syndrome","Polydipsia"]},"chemicalList":{"chemical":[{"name":"Sodium","registryNumber":"9NEZ333N27"},{"name":"Water","registryNumber":"059QF0KO0R"}]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Unpaywall","url":"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/s00508-024-02325-5.pdf"},{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00508-024-02325-5"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC10904443"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC10904443?pdf=render"}]},"commentCorrectionList":{"commentCorrection":[{"id":"39436441","source":"MED","reference":"Wien Klin Wochenschr. 2024 Nov;136(21-22):645. doi: 10.1007/s00508-024-02454-x.","type":"Erratum in","orderIn":1}]},"isOpenAccess":"Y","inEPMC":"Y","inPMC":"Y","hasPDF":"Y","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","citedByCount":3,"hasData":"N","hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasLabsLinks":"Y","license":"cc by","hasEvaluations":"N","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"N","dateOfCompletion":"2024-03-01","dateOfCreation":"2024-02-29","firstIndexDate":"2024-03-01","fullTextReceivedDate":"2025-02-05","dateOfRevision":"2026-01-20","electronicPublicationDate":"2024-02-29","firstPublicationDate":"2024-02-29"}]}}